<title>REPUBLIC OF IRELAND: Adare Printing pre-tax profit up 28 pct.</title>
<headline>Adare Printing pre-tax profit up 28 pct.</headline>
<dateline>DUBLIN 1996-11-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to October 31, 1996</p>
<p>					  (million punts unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr (pence)		30.01		  vs 25.01</p>
<p> Dividend (pence)	 3.12		   vs 2.08</p>
<p> Pretax		     5.20		   vs 4.0</p>
<p> Turnover		   54.95		  vs 34.35</p>
<p> Operating profit	 6.24		   vs 4.28</p>
<p> Net Interest payable   1.01		   vs 0.18</p>
<p> Tax paid		   1.60		   vs 1.12</p>
<p> Net taxed		  3.63		   vs 2.98</p>
<p> Attributable	     3.50		   vs 2.88</p>
<p> Registration date	December 10, 1996</p>
<p> Pay date		   February 7, 1997.</p>
<p> Ex-dividend date	 December 2, 1996.</p>
<p>NOTE - Ireland's Adare Printing Group said it had continued the growth of recent years.</p>
<p>It said while the climate for acquisitions was becoming less favourable due to comparatively high ratings in the market, nevertheless, the Group still saw some opportunities to add shareholder value in attractive sectors.</p>
<p>Adare said the board was confident in the UK economy and optimistic about the future.</p>
<p>-- Dublin newsroom 353 1 660 3377</p>
</text>
